    <!-- Stadium Descriptions -->
    <string name="stadium_desc_metlife">Located in New Jersey, it is one of the largest NFL stadiums and the site of the 2026 World Cup final.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_att">A technological marvel with one of the largest video boards in the world and a retractable roof.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_sofi">The most expensive and modern stadium in the world, located in the Los Angeles region.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_hard_rock">Iconic multi-purpose stadium that has hosted six Super Bowls.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_lumen_field">Known for its vibrant atmosphere and for being the loudest MLS/NFL stadium.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_levis">A sustainable and technological stadium in the heart of Silicon Valley.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_lincoln_financial">A modern stadium that uses solar and wind energy for its operation.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_gillette">Located near Boston, it is the historic home of the New England Patriots.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_nrg">Famous for being the first NFL stadium to have a retractable roof.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_arrowhead">Recorded in Guinness as the loudest open stadium on the planet.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_mercedes_benz">Highlight for its futuristic architecture and roof that opens like a camera lens.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_azteca">The temple of world football, the first stadium to host three World Cups.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_akron">One of Mexico\'s most beautiful stadiums, known for its volcano-shaped design.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_bbva">Called the \"Steel Giant\", it offers a spectacular view of the mountains.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_bmo_field">Canada\'s premier soccer stadium, located on the shore of Lake Ontario.</string>
    <string name="stadium_desc_bc_place">An incredible multi-purpose stadium with a cable-supported retractable roof system.</string>

